    "items": [
      {
        "type": "heading1",
        "verse_numbers": [],
        "lines": [
          "David’s Song of Thanksgiving"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          1
        ],
        "lines": [
          "David spoke the words of this song to the Lord on the day the Lord rescued him from the grasp of all his enemies and from the grasp of Saul."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          2
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He said:",
          "The Lord is my rock, my fortress, and my deliverer,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          3
        ],
        "lines": [
          "my God, my rock where I seek refuge.",
          "My shield, the horn of my salvation, my stronghold, my refuge,",
          "and my Savior, you save me from violence."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          4
        ],
        "lines": [
          "I called to the Lord, who is worthy of praise,",
          "and I was saved from my enemies."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          5
        ],
        "lines": [
          "For the waves of death engulfed me;",
          "the torrents of destruction terrified me."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          6
        ],
        "lines": [
          "The ropes of Sheol entangled me;",
          "the snares of death confronted me."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          7
        ],
        "lines": [
          "I called to the Lord in my distress;",
          "I called to my God.",
          "From his temple he heard my voice,",
          "and my cry for help reached his ears."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          8
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Then the earth shook and quaked;",
          "the foundations of the heavens trembled;",
          "they shook because he burned with anger."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          9
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Smoke rose from his nostrils,",
          "and consuming fire came from his mouth;",
          "coals were set ablaze by it."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          10
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He bent the heavens and came down,",
          "total darkness beneath his feet."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          11
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He rode on a cherub and flew,",
          "soaring on the wings of the wind."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          12
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He made darkness a canopy around him,",
          "a gathering of water and thick clouds."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          13
        ],
        "lines": [
          "From the radiance of his presence,",
          "blazing coals were ignited."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          14
        ],
        "lines": [
          "The Lord thundered from heaven;",
          "the Most High made his voice heard."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          15
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He shot arrows and scattered them;",
          "he hurled lightning bolts and routed them."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          16
        ],
        "lines": [
          "The depths of the sea became visible,",
          "the foundations of the world were exposed",
          "at the rebuke of the Lord,",
          "at the blast of the breath of his nostrils."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          17
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He reached down from on high",
          "and took hold of me;",
          "he pulled me out of deep water."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          18
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He rescued me from my powerful enemy",
          "and from those who hated me,",
          "for they were too strong for me."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          19
        ],
        "lines": [
          "They confronted me in the day of my calamity,",
          "but the Lord was my support."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          20
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He brought me out to a spacious place;",
          "he rescued me because he delighted in me."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          21
        ],
        "lines": [
          "The Lord rewarded me",
          "according to my righteousness;",
          "he repaid me",
          "according to the cleanness of my hands."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          22
        ],
        "lines": [
          "For I have kept the ways of the Lord",
          "and have not turned from my God to wickedness."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          23
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Indeed, I let all his ordinances guide me",
          "and have not disregarded his statutes."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          24
        ],
        "lines": [
          "I was blameless before him",
          "and kept myself from my iniquity."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          25
        ],
        "lines": [
          "So the Lord repaid me",
          "according to my righteousness,",
          "according to my cleanness in his sight."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          26
        ],
        "lines": [
          "With the faithful",
          "you prove yourself faithful,",
          "with the blameless",
          "you prove yourself blameless,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          27
        ],
        "lines": [
          "with the pure",
          "you prove yourself pure,",
          "but with the crooked",
          "you prove yourself shrewd."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          28
        ],
        "lines": [
          "You rescue an oppressed people,",
          "but your eyes are set against the proud —",
          "you humble them."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          29
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Lord, you are my lamp;",
          "the Lord illuminates my darkness."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          30
        ],
        "lines": [
          "With you I can attack a barricade,",
          "and with my God I can leap over a wall."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          31
        ],
        "lines": [
          "God #— #his way is perfect;",
          "the word of the Lord is pure.",
          "He is a shield to all who take refuge in him."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          32
        ],
        "lines": [
          "For who is God besides the Lord?",
          "And who is a rock? Only our God."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          33
        ],
        "lines": [
          "God is my strong refuge;",
          "he makes my way perfect."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          34
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He makes my feet like the feet of a deer",
          "and sets me securely on the heights."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          35
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He trains my hands for war;",
          "my arms can bend a bow of bronze."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          36
        ],
        "lines": [
          "You have given me the shield of your salvation;",
          "your help exalts me."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          37
        ],
        "lines": [
          "You make a spacious place beneath me for my steps,",
          "and my ankles do not give way."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          38
        ],
        "lines": [
          "I pursue my enemies and destroy them;",
          "I do not turn back until they are wiped out."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          39
        ],
        "lines": [
          "I wipe them out and crush them,",
          "and they do not rise;",
          "they fall beneath my feet."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          40
        ],
        "lines": [
          "You have clothed me with strength for battle;",
          "you subdue my adversaries beneath me."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          41
        ],
        "lines": [
          "You have made my enemies retreat before me;",
          "I annihilate those who hate me."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          42
        ],
        "lines": [
          "They look, but there is no one to save them —",
          "they look to the Lord, but he does not answer them."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          43
        ],
        "lines": [
          "I pulverize them like dust of the earth;",
          "I crush them and trample them like mud in the streets."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          44
        ],
        "lines": [
          "You have freed me from the feuds among my people;",
          "you have preserved me as head of nations;",
          "a people I had not known serve me."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          45
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Foreigners submit to me cringing;",
          "as soon as they hear, they obey me."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          46
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Foreigners lose heart",
          "and come trembling from their fortifications."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          47
        ],
        "lines": [
          "The Lord lives #— #blessed be my rock!",
          "God, the rock of my salvation, is exalted."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          48
        ],
        "lines": [
          "God #— #he grants me vengeance",
          "and casts down peoples under me."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          49
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He frees me from my enemies.",
          "You exalt me above my adversaries;",
          "you rescue me from violent men."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          50
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Therefore I will give thanks to you among the nations, Lord;",
          "I will sing praises about your name."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          51
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He is a tower of salvation for his king;",
          "he shows loyalty to his anointed,",
          "to David and his descendants forever."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      }
    ]
  },
